{"author":{"id":"ce771b8a9b8c30a8aac165a8b1cdb0957637d3941276ec4f27335daee16d79de"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794784846,"nonce":"sQ+m84Ti2c3V/bfV0iQJnpRmT/A=","target":"a12b6743cdf6fe79e783f58563e3266a38c91adfb1a7c5f6e2ab1a47b7d18e74","message":"## Parent\n\nSpec: 2fe2dcc — Grow overview redesign. Ticket 02 of 11.\n\n## What to build\n\nRecording a phase transition becomes an ordinary event. A new Phase-change\naction covers the boundaries with no canonical action (into Seedling,\nVegetative, Curing, or back to Germination); picking Flowering maps to a\nFlip and picking Drying to a Harvest, reusing the existing actions. The\nforecast's actuals gain boundary pins for the new action, windows re-anchor\nfrom every pin, and a later Flip or Harvest supersedes a manual pin for the\nsame boundary. This ticket lands the core and API layers with API-level\nverification; the picker UI is the next ticket.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A Phase-change action is accepted through the actions API with an optional backdated date and stores like any action.\n- [ ] A boundary pin shifts its phase window and everything downstream; earlier windows back-fill to fit.\n- [ ] Flip and Harvest pins behave exactly as today (no regression).\n- [ ] A later Flip/Harvest supersedes a manual boundary pin for the boundary it describes; picks are never silently superseded by time passing.\n- [ ] Phase-sensitive outputs (env snapshot, coach, lamp advice) follow the re-anchored phase through the existing endpoints.\n- [ ] Unit and property tests: re-anchor semantics, contiguity and monotonicity under arbitrary pins, event-supersedes-pin rule.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- 01 — Open-ended photoperiod veg (same forecast engine; lands first to avoid colliding edits).","files":null}]}